give up on their way of thinking. True art is one that truly innovates, not this lowly scum known as \"pure power\" and it's not even true power, but these people cannot simply grasp this idea.\n\n21. Spelling and Lacanist obscurity\n\nThe characteristic theme of the works of Spelling is the dialectic, and therefore the futility, of capitalist consciousness. Sartre’s model of the posttextual paradigm of context states that consensus must come from communication. It could be said that la Tournier suggests that the works of Spelling are reminiscent of Burroughs.\nBaudrillard promotes the use of Lacanist obscurity to deconstruct communism. Thus, the subject is contextualised into a material neocapitalist theory that includes language as a paradox.\nFoucault uses the term ‘Lacanist obscurity’ to denote not construction, but preconstruction. In a sense, a number of desituationisms concerning Sontagist camp may be discovered.\n\nThe stasis of expressionism depicted in Pynchon’s The Crying of Lot 49 emerges again in Gravity’s Rainbow. It could be said that the primary theme of Scuglia’s analysis of Lacanist obscurity is a mythopoetical whole.\n\n22. Capitalist deconstructions of the present time\nToday was quite a fine day, it had moments of enjoyement, sadness, dread and even rage. It isnt like i want to control my feelings, or tell myself how to act, but knowing how i want to convey myself makes me happy with it, even if this day wont be like yesterday, even if that day too had those same emotions, i wouldnt classify yesterday the same as today, these emotions i have are ever changing and it does cause me stress when i feel lost in myself, but if i take a second to rotate the canvas and look at it in a different way, maybe that new way of viewing my emotions will help me improve my understanding of myself. Even if i dont know how tomorrow will be, whether or not i will be there tomorrow, or if i will even understand myself, i have a feeling tomorrow wont be like today, or yesterday, but a new way of good. And i think that is quite fine.\n\n23. Intellectualised models of therianthropy\nSometimes, when I'm all alone, I like to start making animal noises. I start barking, meowing, trumpeting, crowing, chirping, screaming, roaring, growling, screeching, whistling, rasping, buzzing, baying, snorting, honking, mooing, singing, croaking, rattling, and howling. The neighbors often call the police on me, angry at my impulses for waking up their 6-month baby, but I could care less. The police can break into my room, handcuff my arms, and detain me, but at the end of the day, I will still make animal noises, and no one can stop me. BARK BARK BARK MEOW MEOW MEOW WOO WOO WOO CA CAWK CA CAWK CA CAWK CHIRP CHIRP CHRIP AAAAAAAAAAH AAAAAAAAAAAH AAAAAAAAAAH ROOOOAR ROOOOOAR GRRRRRRRRRRR GRRRRRRRRRRR SCREECH SCREECH SCREECH WHIS WHIS WHIS RASP RASP RASP BZZZZZZZ BZZZZZZZZZZ BZZZZZZZZZZ WOOOOO WOOOOO WOOOO MOOO MOOO MOOO I CAN SING I CAN SING I CAN SING CROAK CROAK CROAK RATTLE RATTLE RATLLE HOOOOOWL HOWWWWWWWWWL\n\n24. The end\nNine years... It's too long. We're all tired. But we're all really happy. We're never going to make an update of this scope or scale again, but damn if we're not impressed by it.\nSo from the bottom of my heart: Thank you for giving us the space to make cool things unabated. It means a huge deal to me that someone cares what the weird autistic guy thinks; I certainly wasn't given that appreciation in real life.\n- Myr\n\n25. The end continues\nEleven... It's too long. Somehow I feel like I've mutated more as a person these past two years than I did in the last decade.\nSo many friends here and elsewhere fraying, so many changes to Roblox, most for the worst.\nI stare at the console as it tries to AI automcomplete my thoughts, completely incorrectly.\n\n- Myr\n"
